g other  than a small minorities the small  minority we're talking about here  absolutely which is why  the inquiry and the review that the home  secretary announced will do first of all  find out why and how wayne cousins could  have risen through the ranks and  things like the flashing incidents and  all the other  if you like red flags that were going up  why they weren't taken more seriously  secondly it will look at systemic issues  cultural issues  within the police and i'm confident we  will get to the bottom of this and as  justice secretary we will have a we're  already through the uh the the review of  uh rape uh cases and our violence  against women and girls strategy we're  going to look root and branch at  everything from  i'm talking about the experiences of  female  victims and everything from the time it  takes to examine a mobile phone in  evidence right the way through to and  we're already doing this protecting  vulnerable uh victims giving evidence in  court so you don't find that on top of  the appalling ordeal physical and mental  trauma they've been through that the  justice system isn't compounding that  with the way that they're treated so we  will look at everything from top to  bottom  and i  look i've said it's my number one  priority to make sure women feel  confident in the justice system and  confident in being able to walk the  streets without having to look over  their shoulder in fear  let's talk about the the prime minister  the man to whom you are of course in  your new role as deputy prime minister  number two uh what are we to to make of  the the emphasis this week on wage  growth on wage growth as being  not the be all and end all but certainly  an overwhelming priority for the prime  minister  is no one in government concerned  that wage at wage growth goes hand in  hand with an increase in inflation  well look there's clearly as we go  through the pandemic this issue of um  inflation but uh the forecasts show that  uh after t